{"name":"Confidence","hex":"#a98a6b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"confidence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Self-assurance.","A feeling of certainty; firm trust or belief; faith."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confidence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Confidence","blocks":[{"text":"Confidence is the feeling of belief or trust that a person or thing is reliable. Self-confidence is trust in oneself. Self-confidence involves a positive belief that one can generally accomplish what one wishes to do in the future. Self-confidence is not the same as self-esteem, which is an evaluation of one's worth. Self-confidence is related to self-efficacy—belief in one's ability to accomplish a specific task or goal. Confidence can be a self-fulfilling prophecy, as those without it may fail because they lack it, and those with it may succeed because they have it rather than because of an innate ability or skill."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confidence","wikidata":"Q4116378"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bashful_Sturgeon_Bay.jpg/500px-Bashful_Sturgeon_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Bashful_Sturgeon_Bay.jpg/500px-Bashful_Sturgeon_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photo captioned \"Bashful\" in a 1916–1917 yearbook, Sturgeon Bay, Wisconsin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABashful_Sturgeon_Bay.jpg"}],"sounds":{"confidence":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/En-us-confidence.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c4/En-us-confidence.ogg/En-us-confidence.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedi